WEBVTT

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:09.110
If we overlook the fact that you're completely wrong, then you're mostly right.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:15.780
While most of our time on the island was spent as we pleased...

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.030
There was one strict rule.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:25.630
1st Floor, Dining Room

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.290
We all had to eat supper together.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.670
If we treat the table as a clock, Ilia was at twelve.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:01:00.620
In other words, the mansion's owner, Akagami Ilia,
and Kunagisa Tomo were sitting opposite each other.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:06.620
And setting at lucky number seven...was me.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:07.960
Will this work

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.100
Mansion's Head Maid

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:29.480
Twelve of us in all.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.740
Lucky number? In this group?

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:35.070
Nonsense.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:38.320
What meaning could that possibly have?

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.830
I was clearly out of my element.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.330
I didn't belong here.

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:51.630
Not that I'd ever, in all my nineteen years, been some place I belonged.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:59.180
Not in Kobe, not in Houston, not in Kyoto,
and most certainly not on this island.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:03.010
In this great wide world, I was alone.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.100
Not that I minded.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:06.680
I liked being alone.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.480
I'm not just saying that.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.190
Even if I am.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:17.200
Well, since Kunagisa has arrived, let the day's pleasantries begin!

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:19.780
Let us eat.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.040
Everyone, raise your glasses!

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:26.540
Cheers!

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.290
Cheers!

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:37.470
What I lack is everything you have

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:44.640
What I want to be is everything you want

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:48.230
The moment we first met

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.770
I'm sure I already knew

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:56.110
Even before it began

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:59.820
Behind my words

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.820
I'm always hiding

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:08.080
Keeping my feelings buried deep

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:22.050
Now, the world that keeps us trapped sure changes before you know it

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:31.230
I mean my heart's already dyed a single color,
in my mind the answer's already been chosen

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:37.690
Is it fate? I don't know, but I'll reach out my hand

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:41.360
I bet we don't need words at all

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:45.240
Your melody and my rhythm

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:49.870
Clamp up our feelings and spin out our fingers

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:53.210
I'll always be right here

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:59.170
<i>The Beheading Cycle</i>

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:59.170
<i>The Blue Savant and
the Master of Nonsense</i>

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:57.040
Right by your side

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.170
<i>Day 3 (2) Assembly and Arithmetic</i>

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.170
<i>The Beheading Cycle</i>

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:06.510
Sashirono Yayoi.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:12.770
She was running the kitchen at the mansion, but she was no servant.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:17.610
Yes...she was one of the geniuses invited to this island.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.270
I need to block this out

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.270
And some more oh god help

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.270
I need even more rt

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.270
Two more should do it

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.270
Sashirono Yayoi

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.270
Genius Chef

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:27.160
Rumor had it Yayoi had a way to make any dish
taste better than if anyone else alive made it.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:33.000
I'm not like Himena вЂ“ I don't have any supernatural powers.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.830
I trained and practiced to get this good.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:45.090
But my nose and tongue are a little...no, a lot better than most people's.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.510
Like, well...

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:55.060
You're AB?

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:58.940
And Rh negative? Am I right?

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:03.240
You can tell that by tasting my skin?

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.740
Your sweat, actually.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:12.950
My tongue can discriminate between two hundred
thousand flavors at twenty levels of intensity.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.250
My nose about half that, maybe?

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:20.130
That's all I had going for me as a kid.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:23.550
I figured cooking was the only path in life for me.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:36.850
So, our next guest вЂ“ the next genius вЂ“ has been decided.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:52.830
The genius arriving here next week is
more than equal to the present company.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.040
What sort of person is this?

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.620
Hmm...

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:00.130
We've only met once.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:03.380
But...once was enough.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:08.380
I suppose you could say...enough to become my hero.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:13.260
There's no other word for it.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.640
Like the detective in a mystery novel...

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:20.310
Or the monster in a monster movie!

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:22.320
Monster?

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:25.150
Well, that is high praise indeed.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.320
I look forward to it.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.410
Remember the name вЂ“ Aikawa!

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:32.620
It will be such fun.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:36.750
I'm such a big fan of Aikawa.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.080
You could even call it love.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.540
Aikawa, hunh?

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:48.050
Oh! That reminds me, Kunagisa.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:51.390
You're due to leave before that.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.810
Yep. Four more days.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:07:00.600
That is <i>such</i> a shame. This is the opportunity of a lifetime!

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:04.320
I would love for you to meet Aikawa too.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.480
Can nothing be done?

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:12.450
Nope! Where I come from, you never
change your mind once something's decided.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:17.370
They call me the walking, talking schedule. Same goes for Ii-chan.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:20.960
Oh, dear.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:27.760
But, Kunagisa...I'm sure meeting Aikawa would mean a lot to you.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:32.590
A meeting like that...it's sure to provide
inspiration. There's no doubt in my mind!

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:34.260
Inspiration?

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:36.180
Don't be absurd.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:44.110
If you ask me, allowing others to influence you is proof you're inherently mediocre. Average. Talentless.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:46.900
Well, that certainly is an unusual position.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:54.620
For more than five years at the ER3 System,
I was surrounded by the finest minds on the planet.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:58.370
Without that experience, I would not be what I am today.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:04.750
I've been on this island with you for a considerable time now, and I do not feel improved by it one bit.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.630
Quite the opposite, in fact.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:15.260
Human beings are social creatures.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:26.440
Ibuki, people as proud of their independence as you
need to take a good long look at themselves.

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:31.240
I am not particularly proud. I merely
do not waste time with false humility.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:35.870
I simply state things as they are. That's how I choose to live.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:36.820
So you say.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.790
So I say? That trick again?

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:45.420
You think if you avoid stating your opinion
and equivocate you'll make yourself look clever?

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:49.000
Oh, yes, you are such a clever one. You wish!

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.670
My ears hurt.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:56.300
You are being very unpleasant, Kanami, Akane.

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:03.980
I'm sorry. I got carried away.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:06.770
Yeah, my bad.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:11.070
I smell trouble brewing.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.150
Is that a prophecy?

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.910
What kind of trouble, Himena?

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:19.950
I am ever so curious! Please, go on!

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:23.870
No. I have nothing further to say.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:26.460
You see...

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:34.670
I'm not arrogant enough to try and involve myself with the world.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.220
What?

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:41.350
Maki, what does that even mean?

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:45.810
I mean nothing, I'm sure. Just as your actions are utterly without meaning.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:52.820
I see...hmm...you're the kind of guy that gets angry on behalf of others.

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:58.860
Not something I can recommend. It isn't a bad
quality to have, but it's not a good one either.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.780
Oh? Why is that?

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:06.460
I think it's a wonderful thing to be angry for a complete stranger.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:09.960
Not something many people manage these days.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:17.010
People who get emotional for other people also
blame other people for anything that happens to them.

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:21.510
I hate people like you more than anything.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:29.520
You let other people set your course. You're the type
that ignores a traffic signal because everyone else is.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:33.860
Appalling in your own formlessness.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:41.660
The Japanese often speak of harmonizing without
agreeing, but you neither agree nor harmonize.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:46.540
I simply hate people like that. Despise them.

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:52.210
They blame everyone else for everything
and never take personal responsibility.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:57.510
You...you have no right to speak to me like that, Himeno Maki.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:01.010
Are you angry? Your boiling point is awfully low.

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.390
Quick to anger...quick to forget?

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:04.350
Shut the

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:10.020
Ii-chan. This is nothing to get mad about.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:18.360
...I know.

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:26.580
Sorry. I was just joking.

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:41.380
Your turn in the bath.

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:42.510
No!

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:45.800
If not today, take one tomorrow.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:46.810
Don't wanna.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:53.770
2nd Floor, Kunagisa Tomo's Room

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:51.310
You're taking a bath tomorrow if I have to tie you up and throw you in.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.770
Don't want that, do you?

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:59.440
Gross! I wish I was a fish.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:03.280
They never have to take baths.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:05.660
But they must be cold in winter.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:11.120
That reminds me! Stop me if you've heard this.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:14.710
So, say you have some fish in an aquarium, right?

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:20.840
And you raise the temperature of the water little by little.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:24.050
Until eventually the water's boiling!

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:29.600
And the fish won't even notice! They'll just
keep swimming around in boiling water!

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:32.060
Sounds fake, actually true!

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:37.230
Now, Ii-chan, what does this tell us?

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:39.480
Global warming isn't a problem?

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:40.730
Bingo!

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:46.870
That huuurt.

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:49.790
What's wrong with you?

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:52.250
I'm hungry.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:54.670
Didn't you just stuff yourself?

00:12:55.040 --> 00:13:00.210
So what if I did? I didn't eat anything else all day!

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:03.420
I'm sure it wasn't enough.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.550
Come, Ii-chan. Let's go find some food.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.220
Can you put my hair up first?

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:11.930
Yayoi's probably in bed already.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:15.140
She wakes up early, so she must sleep early too.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:22.990
I think Hikari is still up. If she's asleep too than you'll have to cook, Ii-chan!

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.400
Why me?

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:29.450
Watching your back when you cook? Meow!

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:34.250
All right, all right, all right. Whatever you want. As you wish.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.170
Come over here and I'll put your hair up.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:39.380
Okely dokely!

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:41.460
Oh, Tomo!

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:48.800
Welcome to my club.

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:55.770
1st Floor, Living Room

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:55.770
Sorry about before. I guess I hit a nerve.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:14:02.190
I mean it, really. Anyone would be angry. I rubbed you the wrong way.

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:04.610
Not exactly.

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:08.110
Right, it was more getting under your skin.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:14.160
How'd Kanami treat you? You modeled for her and everything?

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.870
Yeah, well. It went okay, I guess.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.290
She's impossible, isn't she?

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.000
I wouldn't say that.

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:27.840
Really? Honestly, I've never met a woman more impossible than her.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:38.100
I thought bringing Kanami to this island, and spending time
in this company...I thought it might be good for her.

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:43.070
But looks like she's gonna be like this the rest of her life.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.980
That's one way to live.

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:48.240
Referring to who?

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:55.240
What brings you to this island, Himena?

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.500
I've been wondering.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:00.460
Hardly an ordinary vacation, is it?

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:04.500
It is a vacation, actually. So easy here.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:10.880
Get paid for living. With net access, I can even do
my fortune telling from here. Marvels of the modern age.

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:13.510
Never had such fun in all my life.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:18.270
She's a parasite. An advanced parasite.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:21.150
Pot calling the kettle black.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:25.690
What the hell did you come here for, anyway?

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:31.610
Don't tell me it's just because Kunagisa
asked you. That would just be stupid.

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:36.910
But forget about you.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:40.660
Kunagisa! Why did you come here?

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:47.130
A whim, nothing more. I barely ever bother
coming up with reasons for the things I do.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:48.840
You sure?

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:55.510
Despite her personality, she doesn't appear to have
any trouble getting along with people besides me.

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:57.970
Because unlike you, they aren't pointless.

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:00.730
Telepathy, hunh?

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:03.230
You sure are amazing, Himeno.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.060
But you do overdo it sometimes.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:11.070
More than a few geniuses have fled the island after a run in with you.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:16.070
I'm only playing, but everyone gets all upset. Psychic discrimination!

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:21.790
Can you prove that you have psychic powers, Maki?

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:24.880
Don't really see the need.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:28.550
Want me to read your fortune again?

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:29.630
No, thanks.

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:34.800
Let me talk about you and Kunagisa. A compatibility reading!

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:40.180
Both of you are people that don't <i>need</i> friends.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:42.810
So why are you together?

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:44.940
What's the reason there?

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:51.280
My, my, this is twisted.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:57.120
You're with Kunagisa because you're incredibly, insanely jealous of her.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:03.290
You envy her ability to express her emotions however she likes.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:08.380
And yet...she doesn't seem at all happy.

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:18.140
She has everything you want and can do everything
you can't but isn't happy вЂ“ what a relief that must be.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:22.390
With her around, you don't care if things don't go your way.

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:24.480
Really?

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:25.730
No.

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:32.230
Maki, it seems you've got the wrong idea
about me. I'm just not that complicated a man.

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:34.820
I'm pretty simple, inside.

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:36.280
Well...

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:39.870
That might be true. And it might not be true.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:41.740
Hey, Maki!

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:45.710
Then why am I with Ii-chan?

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:49.840
Sorry. Can't read your mind or past, Kunagisa.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:53.710
There are people I just can't read.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:56.130
Incompatible or something.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:18:01.510
And those people tend to disrupt the signals off everyone else too.

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:07.690
Now then, our unimaginative friend here distracted me, Kunagisa.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:12.230
But I still haven't heard why you came to this island.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.570
Like I said, a whim.

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:21.410
No...I may not be able to read you, but I can tell that isn't true.

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:25.080
Okay then.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:29.170
I'm interested in a case that happened here a long time ago.

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.210
Remain calm!

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:55.030
Is it over?

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:56.320
It's over.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:18:59.610
An earthquake?

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:03.240
And a big one. What magnitude?

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:07.620
Sorry, Hikari вЂ“ can I borrow the phone?

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.170
I'm worried about Kanami.

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.830
Is there a radio here, Hikari?

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:16.460
To check the magnitude...or Tomo, is it on the net yet?

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:23.140
Magnitude on this island is three or four on the Japanese
scale. Not clear which, since we're in an odd location.

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:26.680
Epicenter's near Maizuru. It was a five there.

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:28.310
How do you know?

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:30.230
I just know, okay?

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:36.150
Kanami's fine.

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:37.900
She's in the studio.

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:45.370
The paint cans she had on a shelf all fell over
and made a mess, but she's uninjured.

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:48.160
Shouldn't you go help?

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.370
She told me not to come.

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:53.880
She's busy working.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.590
On your portrait, actually.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:20:01.300
She says it's turning out well and doesn't want me distracting her.

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:05.390
Almost forgot what earthquakes are like.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:11.640
I hope my computers are okay. I think they are.

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:15.060
You must have had enough cheese by now.

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:17.020
Let's go back.

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:35.000
Goin' to bed now.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:38.420
Being full makes me sleepy.

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:40.880
Ii-chan, take my hair down.

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:43.260
You can do that yourself.

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:48.510
The pigtails are so far back! I'm not that flexible, you know.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:55.060
I could do it, but not without risking serious injury.
I broke my arm the last time I tried.

00:20:57.730 --> 00:21:02.240
Okay, okay. You really are adorable, you know.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:11.580
At least take off the coat. Like I've said over and over and over.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.460
I mean, aren't you hot?

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:17.750
There are memories wrapped up in this coat, so I can't.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:20.300
Memories? Okay.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:23.800
I'm going to my room to sleep.

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:25.630
See you tomorrow.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.350
Hey, Ii-chan!

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:32.100
Let's fool around.

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:33.270
Nope.

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:37.650
Awww. You're no fun. Coward! Chicken! Bwak bwak bwak!

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:38.610
Yeah, yeah.

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:49.120
1st Floor, Storeroom (My Room)

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:02.800
My, my, this is twisted.

00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:09.340
You're with Kunagisa because you're incredibly, insanely jealous of her.

00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:19.020
You envy her ability to express her emotions however she likes.

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:24.360
And yet...she doesn't seem at all happy.

00:22:28.150 --> 00:22:38.620
She has everything you want and can do everything
you can't but isn't happy вЂ“ what a relief that must be.

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:43.750
With her around, you don't care if things don't go your way.

00:22:48.300 --> 00:22:49.630
Read me like a book.

00:22:54.560 --> 00:22:59.560
Kunagisa Tomo was...everything I most wanted to be.

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:04.020
Or, no...not that.

00:23:04.690 --> 00:23:07.360
To me, she was...well...

00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:10.200
Well?

00:23:11.610 --> 00:23:13.200
Then what?

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:16.870
It's all nonsense, anyway.

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:27.210
Day 4

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:38.480
2nd Floor, Ibuki Kanami's Room

00:23:55.910 --> 00:24:01.370
The shape of the world I'd believed in

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:04.790
Spun around when near you

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:08.170
Leaning towards your right

00:24:08.170 --> 00:24:10.630
What I've got in my hands

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:13.510
Is not a dream or nothing

00:24:13.510 --> 00:24:17.180
But there's something somewhere

00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:20.230
Throbbing in my heart

00:24:20.230 --> 00:24:23.140
If the one that you do love

00:24:23.140 --> 00:24:27.480
Agrees to put his arms around you

00:24:27.480 --> 00:24:30.240
Then what was a nebulous hope

00:24:30.240 --> 00:24:34.490
Shatters everything that kept you stable

00:24:34.490 --> 00:24:37.080
We'd once been so hollow

00:24:37.080 --> 00:24:39.910
Trapped inside that little box

00:24:39.910 --> 00:24:43.420
But now we've seen outside that box

00:24:43.420 --> 00:24:46.670
And have no idea where we are.

00:24:47.090 --> 00:24:48.500
That's all.

00:25:02.390 --> 00:25:04.890
Afterimages of our bliss

00:25:04.890 --> 00:25:07.730
Glimpses of the future

00:25:07.730 --> 00:25:11.320
A glance at something fragile

00:25:11.320 --> 00:25:16.160
Those times that we can still laugh together
